   "ResearcherNotesProject": "GC, Aug 2026: As of Nov 2025, ownership of the Block 52 project had shifted yet again, with Petronas controlling 80% and Staatsolie owning 20% through its subsidiary Paradise Oil Company NV. My assumption is that the LNG terminal project will retain same ownership as the gas field itself, but we should double-check this in future updates.\n\nAL Jul2025: \"Wison New Energies (WNE) recently won a detailed feasibility study (DFS) for a newbuild floating liquefied natural gas (FLNG) facility set to work at Block 52. The block’s operator and sole owner is Petronas, since its former partner, ExxonMobil Exploration & Production Suriname, decided to exit the block in late 2024.\"",
